## Appendix C: System Architecture and Software Design

### C.1 Module Block Diagram

```
Data Streams → Ingestion → Encoder (Text/TS → Random Proj.) → 
Field Simulator (Strang / FNO fallback) → Adaptive Layer Allocator → 
Hologram Generator (Neural + GS + Denoiser) → Display Driver → SLM
```

All modules communicate via triple‑buffered ring buffers in GPU pinned memory. CUDA streams enable overlap of field simulation, layer allocation, and hologram generation.

### C.2 Field Solver Pseudo‑code (Strang Splitting)

```
Input: Ψ (complex, 256^3), u (2αp), D, S, dt
Output: Ψ_new

// half-diffusion in Fourier space
Ψ_hat = cufft3d(Ψ, FORWARD)
k2 = wavevectors_squared()  // precomputed
Ψ_hat *= exp(-D * k2 * dt / 2)
Ψ = cufft3d(Ψ_hat, INVERSE)

// advection: uniform drift back-trace with cubic B-spline
offset = -u * dt   // constant offset
Ψ = cubic_bspline_interpolate(Ψ, offset)  // one mem-shift operation

// reaction
Ψ += dt * S

// second half-diffusion
Ψ_hat = cufft3d(Ψ, FORWARD)
Ψ_hat *= exp(-D * k2 * dt / 2)
Ψ_new = cufft3d(Ψ_hat, INVERSE)
```

Because \(\mathbf{u}\) is uniform, interpolation reduces to a single stencil evaluation with precomputed weights.

### C.3 Adaptive Depth‑Layer Allocation Algorithm

```
Input: field Ψ (X,Y,Z), target layers Z_budget
Output: layer indices, depth values

Compute variance map V[z] = Var_{x,y}(|Ψ[x,y,z]|)
Build min-heap of adjacent segments, keyed by merge cost:
    cost(L,R) = max(V[L..R]) - mean(V[L..R])
While num_segments > Z_budget:
    Pop pair with lowest cost, merge segments, update heap
For each segment:
    layer_depth = depth_average(segment)
    layer_field = Ψ averaged over segment depths
Return list of (layer_field, layer_depth)
```

### C.4 Hologram Loop Pseudo‑code

```
For each frame t:
    // Field update with FNO fallback
    if FNO_active and residual_last_check < threshold:
        Ψ = FNO_inference(Ψ_prev, v(t))
    else:
        Ψ = Strang_solver(Ψ_prev, u, D, S(v(t)), dt)
        if t % 60 == 0:
            Ψ_ref = Strang_solver(Ψ_prev, ...)
            res = ||Ψ - Ψ_ref||_2 / ||Ψ_ref||_2
            if res > τ: FNO_active = False
            else: FNO_active = True

    // Adaptive layers
    layers, depths = adaptive_allocation(Ψ, Z_budget=64)

    // Neural hologram
    Φ_nn = neural_network(layers)

    // GS refinement (K iterations from convergence study)
    Φ = Φ_nn
    for k=1..K:
        U_SLM = aperture_mask * exp(i*Φ)
        for each z:
            U_prop = ASM_forward(U_SLM, depths[z])
            U_prop *= target_amplitude[z] / (|U_prop|+ε)
            U_SLM += ASM_inverse(U_prop, depths[z])
        Φ = angle(U_SLM)

    // Speckle denoising
    I_recon = simulated_intensity(Φ)   // via ASM to observation plane
    I_denoised = denoiser_net(I_recon)
    // Update target amplitudes for next frame
    for each z:
        target_amplitude[z] = sqrt(I_denoised at depth z)

    // Quantize and output
    Φ_quant = quantize_8bit(Φ)
    slm_send(Φ_quant)
```

